  "term": "ACPT",
  "definition": "ACPT, or the Auditory Continuous Performance Test, is a test used to check for problems with auditory attention by having a person listen to single words and respond to a specific target word. It can help support the diagnosis of ADD or ADHD in children ages 6 to 11.",
